/*
    UICastBar.uss
    Layout only — base colours come from FishMMO-Theme.uss (.fish-bar).
*/

/*
    The TOP of the bottom-centre block, directly above the mana bar and above the buff/debuff
    strips that sit between the two.

    It was `position: relative; align-self: center`, which made it the first flex item of a
    screen-filling document root and therefore pinned it to the top edge of the screen — and
    above the target frame, with which it collided by 50x10px as soon as either buff strip
    reached twelve icons. The width and centre were already chosen for this block ("220px
    matches .res-bar so the cast bar and the resource bars below it line up as one HUD block");
    only the placement never followed, and the two widths had drifted to 220 against 160.

    200 wide, sitting over the middle bar of the row below it: the resource bars went side by
    side (see the layout note in UIResourceBar.uss) and the middle one — mana — starts at x500,
    which is exactly where this is anchored, at exactly its width.

    bottom:132px is 10px above the buff/debuff strips, whose band starts at 122 (bottom:106 plus
    their 16px icons) and which the user placed here deliberately: bars, then the icons read
    outward from the centre, then the cast bar above both. Every offset in this block is measured
    from the bottom so the whole thing tracks the hotkey bar — itself bottom-anchored — instead
    of drifting with the aspect ratio.
*/
.castbar-root {
    position: absolute;
    left: 500px;
    bottom: 132px;
    width: 200px;
    height: 22px;
}

/* The fill represents remaining cast time; width is driven from C# as a percentage. */
.castbar-fill {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    width: 100%;
    border-radius: 3px;
    background-color: var(--cast);
}

/* Centered cast label drawn on top of the fill. */
.castbar-label {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    -unity-font-style: bold;
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--text-bright);
    text-shadow: 0 1px 2px var(--edge-dark);
}
